# One predeclared exact routing/synthesis diagnostic

Before execution, use only saved base_geometry_result.json (SHA256 b22a3143e5df11e1c15220dbe6f1ac83c1ff623dc2559733cc1c0877e4dbc56f), whose coordinates correspond to L_b=8,Q_mem=3,n_old=2,M=4. No prior inverse or dynamical program is rerun. The new diagnostic may perform exact coordinate, permutation and constant-size rational matrix arithmetic in one invocation.

Selected risks: whether A union X is connected without traversing any D site; whether a single 125-site ray at (6,-6,4) is fresh and has the claimed complete unlisted-edge inventory; whether endpoint words restore all arbitrary-state tensor labels; whether the complex positive logarithm has the claimed sign, phase and zero-amplitude behavior.

Predeclared geometry/permutation procedure: retain all saved original and A coordinates, identify the four clock sites at z=3 in the clock square, add the +x memory ray at the component-2 upper-right corner, and BFS the declared S graph to its root. Enumerate S lexicographically and build every endpoint word. Check each used edge is NN, all intermediate endpoint labels restore, the final permutation exchanges each S/E pair and leaves every D label fixed. Enumerate ALL NN pairs touching S/E and subtract the declared A, A-clock, A-data, clock-cycle and memory edges. Save the complete inventory, paths and compact gate list. Check specifically the extra memory-to-outer-cycle edge; report actual counts, including discrepancies.

Predeclared synthesis input: clock order 0,1,2,3 with pivot3 and target [0,3i/5,-12/25,(48+64i)/125]. It is exactly normalized and its pivot magnitude16/25 exceeds1/4. Use the three rational SU(2) blocks with (a,b)=(0,1),(3i/5,4/5),(-3/5,4/5), then the pivot phase(3+4i)/5. Verify exact output coefficients and each block's unitarity. Embed each N in the full four-state pair, verify N^2=projector onto one excitation, and certify positivity of I+N by its exact principal minors. This checks the algebraic cosine/sine identity, not transcendental waveform execution. Check exact full SWAP from its symmetric/antisymmetric projectors and excitation from its X spectral projectors. Deliberate fixed defects: forward-only first routing word must differ from the target permutation, and reversed hopping sign must differ from the selected target. Preserve their defects; no search for fixtures, parameter sweep or success quota.

Before launch, seal this plan, the derivation, exact code, source manifest and input hashes, and preserve actual code copies. A wrapper writes the launch receipt before starting the child, records interpreter/argv and times, saves stdout/stderr and writes an execution receipt after completion. Post-run analytic edits, if any, receive a complete diff against the contemporaneous source. This is the only scientific invocation; bookkeeping/hash checks are labeled separately. No selected success is an independent proof of the general theorem.
